{"skill":{"slug":"skywork-ppt","displayName":"Skywork PPT"},"version":{"version":"1.0.9","createdAt":1776949188398,"changelog":"**Added support for converting NotebookLM-exported files to editable PPTX.**\n\n- New capability: Convert .pptx or .pdf exported from NotebookLM to fully editable PPTX format (Layer 5).\n- Added script: scripts/run_editable_convert.py to handle the conversion process.\n- Added workflow guide: workflow_convert_editable.md.\n- Updated skill description and workflow to include the new conversion feature.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"workflow_convert_editable.md","size":4013,"sha256":"6c259aaae01bc29c89d4024f1206f214b9d9d64315993dabaebf43063f444c18","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"workflow_edit.md","size":4275,"sha256":"8b8a5338e667bdc25f159869090a7b3c481c0fa4d136b5b02e98e1672d64acd1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"workflow_generate.md","size":9584,"sha256":"bb01fea87d81474e48c4d8e5733be0ac719697b84251e86011d95e0445a00d71","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":10486,"sha256":"c8c1c5dadccb44b2bf5a74a09803c7db568cfa488e255bb4e2378cd15a99f04d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"workflow_local.md","size":3981,"sha256":"053772e68dcf626cc980adfe94cb015c03d55064a89dff3d256cf8abdfe08c40","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"workflow_imitate.md","size":7973,"sha256":"32deb286c8b23612787c776091994541d019cfb78e3dfb8ab2454b6ab5b44c2e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/upload_files.py","size":4900,"sha256":"37908ef4500b25de0f5e57bb641cd47cf302896fb32dbde725dfc6b64ea4448d","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"scripts/parse_file.py","size":6798,"sha256":"81a8532d2dc9115f5bb621bb32a08a51d68a240f2567f9fb0a618c1ece48aa84","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"scripts/skywork_auth.py","size":284,"sha256":"45f2076cdf7ad1da4b905e0c6eb1f7c1e6f49e6ad8381007804229f3ee5094d7","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"scripts/run_editable_convert.py","size":9270,"sha256":"08745b32897857cf8fb8b9db12f615981757b460274f7b1b45f04946c7b07623","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"scripts/run_ppt_write.py","size":15459,"sha256":"e886e4a419d62c3f7be02a63000bcb167c42c48539e1beced6e68e015842ee42","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"scripts/constant.py","size":81,"sha256":"8df746fa20b792a234b602e70d1a80677f20b29c06fd054d23288743bd014e75","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"scripts/web_search.py","size":2493,"sha256":"bcbea115e8f44067160fda5e1ad2bc94a6dfe7dab6d9bf38db66f52dccf96d73","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"scripts/local_pptx_ops.py","size":13562,"sha256":"9261d2f34c2218c420f1047839b0833b609652f8c6cca070829acdceea5cecad","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"references/apikey-fetch.md","size":2693,"sha256":"ec65d21fe505365e286d70c0789c10312874abb6e5c8cff936af32b70e519ae5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2381,"sha256":"8c507d796ca57c337976d12f5d9737eade58e14f3b8d372229f1462fc2c6cf4c","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789181753378,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2e4d8c318e4a3ce9bfee955252c944a582ee54adcb13f67448466ce8efa1acda","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2e4d8c318e4a3ce9bfee955252c944a582ee54adcb13f67448466ce8efa1acda","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086121409},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":42,"checkedAt":1789181753378},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This PowerPoint skill is mostly coherent, but it should be reviewed because it uploads local documents to cloud/public URLs and can modify local/system files without strong safeguards.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill requires SKYWORK_API_KEY and sends prompts, reference text, uploaded files, templates, and source decks to api-tools.skywork.ai/Skywork OSS/CDN; this is purpose-aligned for cloud PPT generation but broad for confidential business documents.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The main environment check always installs an unpinned python-pptx dependency using pip with --break-system-packages into the detected Python interpreter, which can mutate a shared/system Python environment.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The workflows disclose remote processing, but they require web search when conversation content is insufficient and require uploading local PPT/template/source files without a clear per-file consent gate, retention limit, or private-only upload option.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The setup guide suggests storing a long-lived API key in plaintext OpenClaw, shell, or Claude settings and echoing it for verification; local delete/reorder operations also overwrite the original PPTX when no output path is supplied. No backdoor, service, or hidden persistence was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is PowerPoint generation, editing, template imitation, conversion, and local slide operations; the scripts generally support that purpose, though web search and generic PDF/DOCX/image parsing broaden the privacy surface beyond local PPT handling.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending selected prompts and files to Skywork/cloud storage. Avoid confidential decks unless your organization approves that service, use a revocable API key stored in a protected secret store, do not echo the key in logs, run dependencies in a virtual environment, and use explicit output paths or backups for local slide edits.","findings":"[TP4] expected: Web search and file upload are documented workflow helpers for creating slide content, so this is not malicious tool poisoning by itself; it remains a privacy/scoping concern because queries and retrieved content leave the local environment.\n[RA1] expected: The self-modification framing is not supported by the artifacts; the actual behavior is user-PPT overwrite during local delete/reorder operations, which is disclosed but risky as a default.\n[AS1] unexpected: No runtime code reads ~/.claude, ~/.codex, or ~/.gemini; the artifact only gives setup instructions for placing SKYWORK_API_KEY in Claude settings, so this is downgraded to credential-handling guidance.\n[SDI-1] expected: Generic document parsing and web search support the generation workflows, but they expand the skill from local PowerPoint operations into broader remote document and content processing.\n[SDI-2] expected: Uploading reference files, templates, and source decks is part of the cloud-backed workflow and is disclosed in SKILL.md, but the workflows lack explicit per-upload confirmation and clear retention or access controls.\n[SQP-2] expected: The public OSS/CDN upload and plaintext API-key setup are real concerns; they are not hidden, but the artifacts should better warn users before sending or exposing sensitive documents and credentials.\n[LP3] unexpected: The package declares required Python and SKYWORK_API_KEY but does not define a narrow tool boundary; the concern is overbreadth and missing controls rather than evidence of abuse.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: Hardcoded language examples exist, but nearby workflow text instructs the agent to detect the user's language, so this is not a material security concern.\n[RA2] expected: A persistent API key is expected for the Skywork integration, but storing it in shell/config files and printing it to the terminal is weaker than protected secret storage.\n[T08] unexpected: The unpinned pip install with --break-system-packages is unnecessary for safe operation and increases install-time risk.\n[T09] unexpected: The web_search.py filename construction allows query-controlled writes outside its temp directory; download URLs from the backend are also fetched without host, size, or file-type validation. These are implementation flaws, not malicious intent.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789181753378}}}}}